  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Access to HIV Prevention and Treatment for Migrants and their Families in Uzbekistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The legal framework for countering HIV in Uzbekistan includes the Law on Prevention of Diseases Caused by the Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) of 2013 and the Presidential Resolution of 2018. While the Law does not refer to migrants, the Presidential Resolution, which includes the Government Programme on countering the spread of HIV, promotes mandatory HIV testing and pre-departure consultations for labour migrants from Uzbekistan. However, the Programme was envisaged for 2018 only. This means, there is no mechanism of migrant-inclusive programming in the country due to the lack of a policy document on the nexus of migration and HIV. The proposed project therefore aims to contribute to the government&#x2019;s efforts to counter the spread of HIV through a migrant-inclusive approach to HIV policy development and increasing awareness levels of HIV prevention and treatment among migrants and their families. To do so, the project will determine baselines through gender and age-disaggregated set of questions delivered through a KAP survey for migrants and their family members. Furthermore, the project will contribute to awareness-raising on HIV among local communities, particularly spouses of migrants, capacity building of service providers on migrant-inclusive HIV prevention and care, and policy development.</narrative>
  </description>
